        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "refactor(qa): unify live channel runtime hosting",
        "body": "Closes #99699\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nTelegram, Slack, WhatsApp, and Matrix live QA commands used separate runtime hosts. Matrix also lives in its own QA runner plugin, so QA Lab needs an owner-neutral way to discover its adapter without importing plugin-private code.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nEach live runner now contributes an `adapterFactory` on its existing `QaRunnerCliRegistration`. QA Lab resolves those adapters through its existing registry and runs them through the shared suite host. Matrix contributes through the QA runner runtime surface, preserving plugin ownership and forced-exit behavior.\n\nRegistration-only QA runners remain direct-mounted for compatibility. Discord is unchanged. Crabline stays on published 0.1.9 in-process events; recorder polling and capability manifests are not introduced.\n\n## User Impact\n\nProduction channel behavior is unchanged. The four live QA commands now share one adapter lifecycle while keeping channel-specific credentials, scenarios, artifacts, and cleanup in their owning runtimes.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Rebased onto `0869edc23b0d183c9c6d57230fa43d28bce7cdf4` before validation.\n- Focused SDK, registry, host, CLI, and Matrix proof passed 110 tests across four Vitest shards.\n- Docs link and glossary checks, `oxfmt`, and `git diff --check` passed.\n- Codex autoreview is clean with no accepted/actionable findings (0.98 confidence on the final naming/docs delta).\n- Exact-head Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kwq3xx95b3sn4ntcg39hegnv` passed `pnpm check:changed`, including SDK, extension, docs, lint, and import-cycle lanes. Actions run: https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/28714567632\n- The SDK surface report passes without budget changes; `adapterFactory` extends the existing registration rather than adding a second contribution registry.\n",
        "branch": "dallin/wave1-channel-host",
